# Artifact digests are the plain SHA-256 of the file's bytes. Git must not
# rewrite line endings on checkout, or a clone on a CRLF platform would report
# digest drift for artifacts nobody touched. This replaces the newline
# normalisation the digest function used to do, which had the worse property of
# making sha256:<hex> not actually the SHA-256 of the artifact.
* -text

*.py text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
